# 🖼️ Lab 09 – Image Data Augmentation & CNN Generalization

> **Machine Learning Laboratory** | Enhancing image classification performance through data augmentation and Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs).

---

## 📖 Overview

Deep learning models often require large and diverse datasets to achieve high performance. When training data is limited, **image augmentation** provides an effective solution by generating transformed versions of existing images, allowing the model to learn more robust and generalized features.

This laboratory extends the computer vision workflow developed in **Lab 07** and **Lab 08** by introducing image augmentation techniques using **TensorFlow/Keras ImageDataGenerator**. Students will visualize augmented samples, train a CNN using the augmented dataset, and evaluate the model using standard classification metrics.

The laboratory consists of two Jupyter notebooks covering both augmentation techniques and CNN training.

---

## 🎯 Learning Outcomes

After completing this laboratory, students will be able to:

- Understand the importance of image augmentation in deep learning
- Apply image transformations using **ImageDataGenerator**
- Generate diverse training samples through augmentation
- Visualize augmented images
- Train CNN models using augmented datasets
- Improve model generalization and reduce overfitting
- Monitor training and validation performance
- Evaluate image classification models using confusion matrices and classification reports

